==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The first two enemies are easy to defeat if you have made it this far. However, Kang Roo has slightly more range than Shadow Boxer K, which means [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] won't hit all the Kang Roos easily, but the stage should be doable regardless with good meatshielding and a well-timed Awakened Bahamut.

You should stall the Kang Roos with some meatshields to have enough money to rush down the stage with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and stackable DPS units such as [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]], who doubles as a [[:Category:Barrier Breaker Cats|Barrier Breaker]] for the UltraBaaBaa in Chapter 2. If one has [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], they can weaken the Shadow Boxer K to help your units survive for longer. [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] can also deal some serious damage to the Kang Roos, even when the former is untalented.

==='''Chapter 2 '''===
Beware of the UltraBaaBaa and bring a Barrier Breaker [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]], primarily the aforementioned [[Li'l Macho Legs Cat|Li'l Macho Legs]], [[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]], event units like [[Tasmanian Giant Crab (Special Cat)|Tasmanian Giant Crab CC]], or use the Breakerblast Cannon. Otherwise, the stage is as trivial as the last one using a similar strategy, just with a Barrier Breaker.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage happens to appear more daunting than it actually is, but with [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] or two Sm Attack Combos and all Anti-Starred Alien treasures up to this point, this stage is fairly easy. Similar strategies from Chapter 1 can be used for Chapter 3, as the enemies are practically unchanged aside from magnifications. No boosting on Mythics is necessary, but boosting Dancer is helpful. No talents on him are needed either.

